title: Will the CUP run for the Spanish General Election?
subtitle: The anti-capitalist formation decides now
view-if: next_spanish_election_time - time <= 5 and cup_parlament_s > 0 and not cup_in_jxsi and not cup_in_jxcat
tags: event
new-page: true
face-image: img/events/cup_congreso.webp 
go-to: player_cup if player_party = "cup"; not_player if player_party != "cup"
role: event

= The ​CUP decides weather to run for the Congreso

@player_cup

TODO!

- @post_event: TODO


@not_player

To run or not to run for the Spanish General Election has been, until quite recently, not even a question for the CUP. The party position has always been that they have nothing to do in Madrid, being there at *"foreign country"*. Now, nonetheless some currents in the party are, at the very least, floating the idea. The main goal being to block decision-making in the Congreso and, by making Spain more difficult to govern, strengthen the hand of the independence moment. Needless to say, this does not convince everyone, and the debate is very much open. [? if spa_fr_active: If they do end up running, we can expect the FR to fold into their candidacy and join efforts. ?]

- @cup_no_run
- @cup_run

@cup_no_run
title: The CUP refuses to run for the Congreso
subtitle: The historical party line is maintained.
choose-if: cup_faction != "Poble Lliure" or cup_parlament_s <= 3 or independence_movement <= 75
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cup_faction = "Poble Lliure": With Poble Lliure currently holding so much power within the CUP, they will be pushing for actually running. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.spa_cup_active = false;
    if (Q.cup_congreso_catalunya_support > 0) {
        Q.erc_congreso_catalunya_support += 0.1*Q.cup_congreso_catalunya_support;
        Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_congreso_catalunya_support"] += 0.05*Q.cup_congreso_catalunya_support;
        if (Q.iu_in_up) {
            Q.up_congreso_catalunya_support += 0.05*Q.cup_congreso_catalunya_support;
        } else {
            Q.podemos_congreso_catalunya_support += 0.05*Q.cup_congreso_catalunya_support;
        }
        Q.abstain_congreso_catalunya_support += 0.8*Q.cup_congreso_catalunya_support;
        Q.cup_congreso_catalunya_support = 0;
    }
!}

Following the historical party line, the CUP will not be running for the Congreso, even if it is to the dismay of factions like Poble Lliure. 

@cup_run
title: The CUP will run for the Congreso!
subtitle: [? if spa_cup_active: The anti-capitalist formation will again be there in the ballots. ?][? if not spa_cup_active: The anti-capitalist formation will break with its historical position. ?][? if cup_faction = "Third Sector": It will take a bit of convincing though. \[-1 resources\] ?]
choose-if: (cup_faction = "Poble Lliure" or (cup_faction = "Third Sector" and (cup_relations > 55 and party_resources >= 1) or spa_fr_active)) and cup_parlament_s > 3 and independence_movement > 75
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cup_faction = "Endavant": With Endavant currently holding so much power within the CUP, this is basically ruled out. ?][? if cup_parlament_s <= 3: The party feels like it lacks the popular support for such a move. ?][? if cup_faction != "Endavant" and not spa_fr_active: [? if cup_relations <= 55: We don't have good enough relations with the CUP. ?][? if party_resources < 1: Not enough resources. ?]?]
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.cup_faction != "Poble Lliure" && !Q.spa_fr_active) {
        Q.party_resources -= 1;
    }
    
    if (!Q.spa_cup_active) {
        G.spaSupportInject(Q, 'cup', 'catalunya', 4.0, 'abstain');
    }
    if (Q.spa_fr_active) {
        Q.cup_congreso_catalunya_support += Q.fr_congreso_catalunya_support;
        Q.fr_congreso_catalunya_support = 0;
    }
    Q.spa_fr_active = false;
    Q.spa_cup_active = true;
!}

The anti-capitalist will be running for the Congreso after all! This positioning, of course, does not make everyone happy, specially those around the Endavant faction. But in any case, we will be seeing them in the General Election ballots soon.

- @post_event: Let's see how they fare...